Z||000026||Tonker||08-17-2001||07:01 PM||||Hey Heather,<P>Is Johnson's beach as disgusting as I've heard it is? I used to swim there all the time. Saw Centennial beach when I was there last month, it still looks nice. My aunt and Uncle have a cottage near Wasaga too, there's some nice roads around there for driving, and the area is gorgeous!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000027||FieroHeather||08-17-2001||11:24 PM||||Hiya Tonker!<P>I havent been out to Johnson's beach in a LONG time...I mainly stick to Centennial or tour around to Minet's Point.  It is a nice road to drive around, and blading it is fun too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I actually havent been swiming at Wasaga or any beach this summer AT ALL!  The only time I was out swimming was when I went with friends to Canada's Wonderland and a Darrien Lake.  I'll be going to Cedar Point pretty soon too.  <P>I constantly drive back and forth to Stayner to take my sister to work or to pick her up, and Im always tempted to just keep on cruisin to Wasaga.  I mean, I am soooooo close, so why not! I guess my work schedule has been TOTALLY bogging up my free time to do that.  Oh well!  At least Im paying for school  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
